WATCH OUT

  - Claim the paths you edit in the shared clone. See AGENTS.md for lane
    scopes, version bumps and tests. CHECKLISTS.md is a separate shared
    claim when minting TCK IDs.
  - Lb is a lead line: it takes one content row at the top of the pager
    and reduces the numbered-line range shown there by one. Pager row
    and scroll assertions must account for it.
  - Escaped href="..." inside a pre block still trips the corpus link
    checker. Use &quot; around the example attribute value.
  - Generated corpus indexes trail page commits by one; commit them after
    the pages, then rerun make corpus.
  - A page title belongs in <title> and the breadcrumb only. Do not add a
    body heading that repeats the breadcrumb; start with an intro paragraph.
    The root guide index has no breadcrumb and keeps its <h1>.
  - make corpus regenerates glossary hubs from tools/glossary_index.py, so
    heading changes there must be made in the generator too.
  - Tamlinux's desktop plan is its own compositor, tam-pane. Sway and
    wlroots are peer projects or technical examples, not targets.
  - Tamlinux's host/rootstock/bud/scion/cultivar/fruit naming is a
    botanical analogy, not a set of plant names.
  - Digit-leading glossary titles belong in glossary/numeric/, not in the
    letter folder matching a later "b" or other letter.
  - Command and corpus versions are independent; W122 is command only.
  - UBSan output in a PTY corrupts the pager screen model; log it to a
    file when testing under sanitizers.
  - work/history/ is read-only; new sessions use work/W<n>-<name>.
  - make dev is Fred's loop; agents do not run it. Do not install a build
    as a side effect of content changes.
